hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1402","He said: Muhammad bin Bashar narrated to us the news of Qubaisa, Muadh bin Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abu Qulabah, on the authority of Qubaisa Al-Bajli, he said: The sun eclipsed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs until it set, then he said: “The sun and the moon will not eclipse.” Because of the death of someone, but they are two of His creation, and God causes whatever He wills to His creation. Then, when God, Blessed and Most High, is revealed to any of His creation He humbled himself before him, so whichever of them humbled, pray until he is delivered or God happens to him.”"
"1403","Abu Bakr said: “As for the news of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, we also narrated to Bundar, he said: Abdul Wahhab narrated to us, Ayoub narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he mentioned the hadith and said: “ So when God reveals himself to any of His creation, He submits to it.”"
"1404","Narrated by Bundar, narrated by Abd al-Wahhab, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of al-Nu’man bin Bashir, similar to the hadith of Ayyub"
